#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192656 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192587 :question/id #uuid "f20f46d9-b799-57a2-90bc-12e6593e8655" :question/math-academy-id "e-13999" :question/problem "Find the solution $(x,y)$ to the following system of equations using the elimination method:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+3y=8 \\\\ x-2y=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $x$ in the first equation is $2,$ while in the second equation it is $1.$\n\nIf we multiply the second equation by $-2,$ then the $x$-coefficient will become $-2,$ which will cancel with the coefficient of $2$ in the first equation.\n![](images/a7/a7e5f9f09d67dd14a4797e5675585973e3aafeb1ee96e9021d245f49ce9c1c7e.svg)\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $x$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\cancel{2x}+3y & =8 \\\\ \\cancel{-2x}+4y & =6 \\\\ (3y+4y) & =(8+6) \\\\ 7y & =14 \\\\ y & =2\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $y = 2.$ However, we still need to find $x.$ To do this, we substitute $y = 2$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}x-2y & =-3 \\\\ x-2(2) & =-3 \\\\ x-4 & =-3 \\\\ x & =1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=1, \\,y=2,$ which can be expressed as $(1,2).$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2dbf4e1a-2c87-562d-8c4d-41fd32e79b86" :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509123 :question-generator/id #uuid "a2ef49f5-dfc4-5fb1-b890-7cb7bc96039a" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186192656.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193226 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f9dc4fdb-fc7f-57b9-bbcb-171440bb6b43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-5,-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191189} {:answer/id #uuid "7891246f-146f-5da4-be15-343b7425f61f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-5,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508564} {:answer/id #uuid "8468d23b-6f42-50bf-9e79-d910d35e0ee2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4,5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508587} {:answer/id #uuid "ac47150e-5e39-5c69-9314-ddb4609e8210" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-5,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508651} {:answer/id #uuid "f55c1c33-5ff5-5f10-90f5-08f56a27906c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-5,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508791}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f9dc4fdb-fc7f-57b9-bbcb-171440bb6b43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-5,-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191189} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d02a81e-fa71-57d8-a298-b58e206ffcea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191187}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4c0138a9-c275-57a0-80c9-430f32b2f421" :question/math-academy-id "q-18787" :question/problem "Find the solution $(x,y)$ to the following system of equations using the elimination method:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}4x-5y=0 \\\\ 2x-3y=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Hint: Eliminate the variable $x.$*" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the $x$-coefficient in the first equation is $4,$ while in the second equation it is $2.$ \n\nIf we multiply the second equation by $-2,$ then the $x$-coefficient will become $-4,$ which will cancel with the coefficient of $4$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}4x-5y=0 \\\\ (\\,2x-3y=2\\,)\\,\\times (-2)\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}4x-5y=0 \\\\ -4x+6y=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $x$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\cancel{4x}-5y & =0 \\\\ -\\cancel{4x}+6y & =-4 \\\\ (-5y+6y) & =(0-4) \\\\ y & =-4\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $y=-4.$ However, we still need to find $x.$ To do this, we substitute $y=-4$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}4x-5y & =0 \\\\ 4x-5(-4) & =0 \\\\ 4x+20 & =0 \\\\ 4x & =-20 \\\\ x & =-5\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=-5,\\,y=-4,$ which can be expressed as $(-5,-4).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193236 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/id #uuid "1baa2398-4954-5c79-9541-1319e47e02cd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191226} {:answer-field/id #uuid "652cda5c-8a31-5ce3-bccf-786c2da038cc" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191227}] :question/id #uuid "96c8f94a-3d88-537c-8d5d-fa47a28c510f" :question/math-academy-id "q-208816" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n${4x + 3y = 5; - x + 7y =-9$\n\nFind the solution $(x, y)$ to this system by eliminating the variable $x$.\n\nThe solution is $($\n{{field-1}} $$,\n{{field-2}}\n$)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508926 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9dddb3dd-6633-5329-a169-4b39e35735ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508628}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9dddb3dd-6633-5329-a169-4b39e35735ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508628} :answer-field/id #uuid "2696769d-e344-58f2-b122-e8524fb62262" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508826} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5032cf38-f7e1-5f19-b56e-8d84bbbcec8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508509}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5032cf38-f7e1-5f19-b56e-8d84bbbcec8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508509} :answer-field/id #uuid "2adc4195-f1d2-500e-8a09-82e4a8b25e53" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508827}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4775db8b-54b5-507a-83b4-6fee15253323" :question/math-academy-id "q-238082" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}6x+13y=21 \\\\ 2x+6y=12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution $(x,y)$ to this system is $($\n{{field-1}}$\\,,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $x$ in the  first  equation is $6,$ while in the second equation it is $2.$ \n\nIf we multiply the second equation by $-3,$ then the $x$-coefficient will become $-6,$ which will cancel with the coefficient of $6$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}6x+13y=21 \\\\ (\\,2x+6y=12\\,)\\,\\times (-3)\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}6x+13y=21 \\\\ -6x-18y=-36\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $x$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\cancel{6x}+13y & =21 \\\\ -\\cancel{6x}-18y & =-36 \\\\ (13y-18y) & =(21-36) \\\\ -5y & =-15 \\\\ y & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $y=3.$ However, we still need to find $x.$ To do this, we substitute $y=3$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x+13y & =21 \\\\ 6x+13(3) & =21 \\\\ 6x+39 & =21 \\\\ 6x & =-18 \\\\ x & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=-3,\\,y=3,$ which can be expressed as $(-3,3).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509050 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b5ee4058-4cb0-5815-af4f-31cb5f7f4b9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509104}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b5ee4058-4cb0-5815-af4f-31cb5f7f4b9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509104} :answer-field/id #uuid "491f86ca-62f3-5ea9-8428-178689de26c2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509073} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "accbd167-8445-5f77-b722-a480de8d9a7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509102}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "accbd167-8445-5f77-b722-a480de8d9a7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509102} :answer-field/id #uuid "a0ddcf7e-8326-53ea-93be-7d843009b320" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509096}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "02c41293-f116-502f-be60-22954dd650e1" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n$\\{-8x + 5y = 1; -2x - 7y = 25$\n\nFind the solution $(x, y)$ to this system by eliminating the variable $x$.\n\nThe solution is $($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$)$." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $x$ in the first equation is $-8$, while in the second equation it is $-2$.\n\nIf we multiply the second equation by $-4$, then the $x$-coefficient will become $8$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $-8$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n\\{-8x + 5y = 1; (-2x - 7y = 25) \\cdot (-4)\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $x$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-8x + 5y &= 1 \\\\\n8x + 28y &= -100 \\\\\n(5y + 28y) &= (1 - 100) \\\\\n33y &= -99 \\\\\ny &= -3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $y = -3$. However, we still need to find $x$. To do this, we substitute $y = -3$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-2x - 7y &= 25 \\\\\n-2x - 7(-3) &= 25 \\\\\n-2x + 21 &= 25 \\\\\n-2x &= 4 \\\\\nx &= -2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=-2, \\,y=-3$, which can be expressed as $(-2,-3)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509058 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "72fa66fd-476b-567c-997f-57d2e464fff5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{737}{36}, - \\frac{79}{18})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509085} {:answer/id #uuid "738e474f-8d81-5bf6-bc84-52f4e7d52157" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(17, 3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509086} {:answer/id #uuid "bd5dcb71-ce6e-543f-8d84-cd26efc72f79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{113}{9}, - \\frac{11}{9})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509105} {:answer/id #uuid "c9adc298-4dc0-5aaf-b90e-98f63bda9ce1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(77, -27)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509110} {:answer/id #uuid "cd44a84c-9d0c-5c1f-a7ba-d0979b60fd66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2, 3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509112}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd44a84c-9d0c-5c1f-a7ba-d0979b60fd66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2, 3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509112} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b8157cd-7759-5311-a70d-1e44f2700470" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509083}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "258cf739-9da3-523a-9e45-9eb6c6ac19c9" :question/problem "Find the solution $(a, b)$ to the following system of equations using the elimination method:\n\n$\\{2a + 5b = 19; 14a - b = 25$\n\n*Hint: Eliminate the variable $a$.*" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $a$ in the first equation is $2$, while in the second equation it is $14$.\n\nIf we multiply the first equation by $-7$, then the $a$-coefficient will become $-14$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $14$ in the second equation.\n\n$$\n\\{(2a + 5b = 19) \\cdot (-7); 14a - b = 25\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $a$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-14a - 35b &= -133 \\\\\n14a - b &= 25 \\\\\n(-35b - b) &= (-133 + 25) \\\\\n-36b &= -108 \\\\\nb &= 3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $b = 3$. However, we still need to find $a$. To do this, we substitute $b = 3$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2a + 5b &= 19 \\\\\n2a + 5(3) &= 19 \\\\\n2a + 15 &= 19 \\\\\n2a &= 4 \\\\\na &= 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $a=2, \\,b=3$, which can be expressed as $(2,3)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509066 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "079d8e57-e723-5341-8dde-001d8b14de99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509052}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "079d8e57-e723-5341-8dde-001d8b14de99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509052} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa48b9e4-f99c-585d-9f9c-fcfbc501054e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509101} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "338fa4ef-f1d5-5f60-94f0-02b5a1eb96c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509064}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "338fa4ef-f1d5-5f60-94f0-02b5a1eb96c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509064} :answer-field/id #uuid "dc5d5aa6-a936-5fba-8da0-69bd505be987" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509117}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "3584fccc-ff52-560b-affb-117ca9035e1b" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n$\\{12s - t = -10; 2s - 5t = 8$\n\nFind the solution $(s, t)$ to this system by eliminating the variable $s$.\n\nThe solution is $($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$)$." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $s$ in the first equation is $12$, while in the second equation it is $2$.\n\nIf we multiply the second equation by $-6$, then the $s$-coefficient will become $-12$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $12$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n\\{12s - t = -10; (2s - 5t = 8) \\cdot (-6)\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $s$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n12s - t &= -10 \\\\\n-12s + 30t &= -48 \\\\\n(-t + 30t) &= (-10 - 48) \\\\\n29t &= -58 \\\\\nt &= -2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $t = -2$. However, we still need to find $s$. To do this, we substitute $t = -2$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2s - 5t &= 8 \\\\\n2s - 5(-2) &= 8 \\\\\n2s + 10 &= 8 \\\\\n2s &= -2 \\\\\ns &= -1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $s=-1, \\,t=-2$, which can be expressed as $(-1,-2)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509068 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a1f2ef5d-7d4c-5874-a963-39537f63090c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509097}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a1f2ef5d-7d4c-5874-a963-39537f63090c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509097} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ad33376-4060-5d96-9e58-c7394afcbf4f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509075} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f7d55bbb-17db-553d-bf14-bb89392e7ac8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509120}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f7d55bbb-17db-553d-bf14-bb89392e7ac8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509120} :answer-field/id #uuid "a4fe934f-8389-5fa9-ac8c-55f6141852fe" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509099}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "3848697a-49af-57cf-80a1-3aeaa90cbfd0" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n$\\{2x + 3y = 1; 14x - 3y = -17$\n\nFind the solution $(x, y)$ to this system by eliminating the variable $x$.\n\nThe solution is $($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$)$." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $x$ in the first equation is $2$, while in the second equation it is $14$.\n\nIf we multiply the first equation by $-7$, then the $x$-coefficient will become $-14$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $14$ in the second equation.\n\n$$\n\\{(2x + 3y = 1) \\cdot (-7); 14x - 3y = -17\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $x$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-14x - 21y &= -7 \\\\\n14x - 3y &= -17 \\\\\n(-21y - 3y) &= (-7 - 17) \\\\\n-24y &= -24 \\\\\ny &= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $y = 1$. However, we still need to find $x$. To do this, we substitute $y = 1$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2x + 3y &= 1 \\\\\n2x + 3(1) &= 1 \\\\\n2x + 3 &= 1 \\\\\n2x &= -2 \\\\\nx &= -1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=-1, \\,y=1$, which can be expressed as $(-1,1)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509081 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "364f9c8a-cb70-5cde-84ad-03c48868d69b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509067}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "364f9c8a-cb70-5cde-84ad-03c48868d69b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509067} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ae32b84-e095-5a2f-9172-81edb43c515f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509094} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30017ff9-b626-5f0f-96bf-3f60d887385e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509061}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "30017ff9-b626-5f0f-96bf-3f60d887385e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509061} :answer-field/id #uuid "c437e509-1b3a-5a4b-872f-05ce93198e77" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509107}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "66c662cf-af7a-5ce7-907d-2fc15145c8ec" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n$\\{9a + 4b = 16; -3a - 4b = 8$\n\nFind the solution $(a, b)$ to this system by eliminating the variable $a$.\n\nThe solution is $($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$)$." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $a$ in the first equation is $9$, while in the second equation it is $-3$.\n\nIf we multiply the second equation by $3$, then the $a$-coefficient will become $-9$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $9$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n\\{9a + 4b = 16; (-3a - 4b = 8) \\cdot (3)\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $a$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n9a + 4b &= 16 \\\\\n-9a - 12b &= 24 \\\\\n(4b - 12b) &= (16 + 24) \\\\\n-8b &= 40 \\\\\nb &= -5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $b = -5$. However, we still need to find $a$. To do this, we substitute $b = -5$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-3a - 4b &= 8 \\\\\n-3a - 4(-5) &= 8 \\\\\n-3a + 20 &= 8 \\\\\n-3a &= -12 \\\\\na &= 4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $a=4, \\,b=-5$, which can be expressed as $(4,-5)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509087 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f96d8b6a-e305-583b-9f12-0bde0306eb41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509121}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f96d8b6a-e305-583b-9f12-0bde0306eb41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509121} :answer-field/id #uuid "4abb445a-53b1-5dac-8db1-19d2b720a47b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509074} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6af2d8cd-fb27-51d6-805e-b4b55efe8db1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509082}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6af2d8cd-fb27-51d6-805e-b4b55efe8db1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509082} :answer-field/id #uuid "d13464d6-06b5-572e-a588-9d420ee2218d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509113}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7b0730ae-94df-51c2-9122-80a657d5c130" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n$\\{6s + 7t = -17; -s + 5t = 9$\n\nFind the solution $(s, t)$ to this system by eliminating the variable $s$.\n\nThe solution is $($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$)$." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $s$ in the first equation is $6$, while in the second equation it is $-1$.\n\nIf we multiply the second equation by $6$, then the $s$-coefficient will become $-6$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $6$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n\\{6s + 7t = -17; (-s + 5t = 9) \\cdot (6)\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $s$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n6s + 7t &= -17 \\\\\n-6s + 30t &= 54 \\\\\n(7t + 30t) &= (-17 + 54) \\\\\n37t &= 37 \\\\\nt &= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $t = 1$. However, we still need to find $s$. To do this, we substitute $t = 1$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-s + 5t &= 9 \\\\\n-s + 5(1) &= 9 \\\\\n-s + 5 &= 9 \\\\\ns &= -4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $s=-4, \\,t=1$, which can be expressed as $(-4,1)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509093 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "64612dae-60be-5da8-a58f-b92a90c02672" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509080}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "64612dae-60be-5da8-a58f-b92a90c02672" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509080} :answer-field/id #uuid "25eacce8-21cd-5065-b87b-8364d07c64a2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509059} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e23b228-36a0-5619-a7b7-a3921c993c40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509053}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e23b228-36a0-5619-a7b7-a3921c993c40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509053} :answer-field/id #uuid "82814543-c725-5b0a-b1ee-c015e7918acc" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509088}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9719f6ce-a725-5fda-8dba-4e72f19011f6" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n$\\{8x + y = -12; 2x - 7y = -32$\n\nFind the solution $(x, y)$ to this system by eliminating the variable $x$.\n\nThe solution is $($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$)$." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $x$ in the first equation is $8$, while in the second equation it is $2$.\n\nIf we multiply the second equation by $-4$, then the $x$-coefficient will become $-8$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $8$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n\\{8x + y = -12; (2x - 7y = -32) \\cdot (-4)\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $x$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n8x + y &= -12 \\\\\n-8x + 28y &= 128 \\\\\n(y + 28y) &= (-12 + 128) \\\\\n29y &= 116 \\\\\ny &= 4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $y = 4$. However, we still need to find $x$. To do this, we substitute $y = 4$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2x - 7y &= -32 \\\\\n2x - 7(4) &= -32 \\\\\n2x - 28 &= -32 \\\\\n2x &= -4 \\\\\nx &= -2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=-2, \\,y=4$, which can be expressed as $(-2,4)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509100 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22b8f003-4864-5c70-95fe-d2b3563f85ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-7, -2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509056} {:answer/id #uuid "329f0e6d-30d3-5076-b0f7-a3bfcc97b663" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{5}{4}, - \\frac{3}{4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509063} {:answer/id #uuid "3d9aae26-9eaa-543f-ad73-d4b0cc4ce5d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- \\frac{29}{5}, \\frac{8}{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509069} {:answer/id #uuid "52ca360c-fb47-5f69-899f-de261ec2a7c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{11}{4}, - \\frac{5}{4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509077} {:answer/id #uuid "f52d4e69-0b6e-526b-ab03-608e96f2bffd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5, -2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509118}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f52d4e69-0b6e-526b-ab03-608e96f2bffd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5, -2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509118} :answer-field/id #uuid "4740f935-4cde-5928-81e3-2873eb56ade9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509072}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a75817b8-4e26-5edd-a706-c4d036e41293" :question/problem "Find the solution $(a, b)$ to the following system of equations using the elimination method:\n\n$\\{-5a - 7b = -11; -a - 3b = 1$\n\n*Hint: Eliminate the variable $a$.*" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $a$ in the first equation is $-5$, while in the second equation it is $-1$.\n\nIf we multiply the second equation by $-5$, then the $a$-coefficient will become $5$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $-5$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n\\{-5a - 7b = -11; (-a - 3b = 1) \\cdot (-5)\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $a$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-5a - 7b &= -11 \\\\\n5a + 15b &= -5 \\\\\n(-7b + 15b) &= (-11 - 5) \\\\\n8b &= -16 \\\\\nb &= -2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $b = -2$. However, we still need to find $a$. To do this, we substitute $b = -2$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-a - 3b &= 1 \\\\\n-a - 3(-2) &= 1 \\\\\n-a + 6 &= 1 \\\\\na &= 5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $a=5, \\,b=-2$, which can be expressed as $(5,-2)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509103 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04912936-0284-538a-a031-970ac8ce1261" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- \\frac{1077}{16}, \\frac{123}{8})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509051} {:answer/id #uuid "305a3950-6485-5d6d-9a0b-5b40b1148ce8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- \\frac{1257}{41}, \\frac{201}{41})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509062} {:answer/id #uuid "4372d300-0380-515a-a5b7-c7ff3a05051f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-24, -3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509071} {:answer/id #uuid "86db7400-28e3-565a-b953-d96d40f7af0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-3, -3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509090} {:answer/id #uuid "fc181fc8-9703-58c0-a004-a3247d964adb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- \\frac{1569}{82}, \\frac{66}{41})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509122}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "86db7400-28e3-565a-b953-d96d40f7af0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-3, -3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509090} :answer-field/id #uuid "891fd9c0-9987-5b47-b883-682276b9d5c4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509091}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b3065a5a-e33d-5a8d-955c-b55d1f00fd62" :question/problem "Find the solution $(x, y)$ to the following system of equations using the elimination method:\n\n$\\{-12x - y = 39; -2x - 7y = 27$\n\n*Hint: Eliminate the variable $x$.*" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $x$ in the first equation is $-12$, while in the second equation it is $-2$.\n\nIf we multiply the second equation by $-6$, then the $x$-coefficient will become $12$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $-12$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n\\{-12x - y = 39; (-2x - 7y = 27) \\cdot (-6)\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $x$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-12x - y &= 39 \\\\\n12x + 42y &= -162 \\\\\n(-y + 42y) &= (39 - 162) \\\\\n41y &= -123 \\\\\ny &= -3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $y = -3$. However, we still need to find $x$. To do this, we substitute $y = -3$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-2x - 7y &= 27 \\\\\n-2x - 7(-3) &= 27 \\\\\n-2x + 21 &= 27 \\\\\n-2x &= 6 \\\\\nx &= -3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=-3, \\,y=-3$, which can be expressed as $(-3,-3)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509106 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c67e1be-bd46-5ffa-8808-2973f101d188" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509079}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5c67e1be-bd46-5ffa-8808-2973f101d188" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509079} :answer-field/id #uuid "83a992ad-facb-5e3e-9fe4-d815a0ee6bea" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509089} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a45d5d1a-0ddd-57b6-94a4-fadb72cadada" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509098}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a45d5d1a-0ddd-57b6-94a4-fadb72cadada" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509098} :answer-field/id #uuid "c9a7d8bf-c851-5b7c-950c-16ced188e9d5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509109}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c26af310-f3be-5785-a8b6-74feb81edc70" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n$\\{21u - 4v = -25; 3u + v = -2$\n\nFind the solution $(u, v)$ to this system by eliminating the variable $u$.\n\nThe solution is $($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$)$." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $u$ in the first equation is $21$, while in the second equation it is $3$.\n\nIf we multiply the second equation by $-7$, then the $u$-coefficient will become $-21$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $21$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n\\{21u - 4v = -25; (3u + v = -2) \\cdot (-7)\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $u$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n21u - 4v &= -25 \\\\\n-21u - 7v &= 14 \\\\\n(-4v - 7v) &= (-25 + 14) \\\\\n-11v &= -11 \\\\\nv &= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $v = 1$. However, we still need to find $u$. To do this, we substitute $v = 1$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n3u + v &= -2 \\\\\n3u + (1) &= -2 \\\\\n3u + 1 &= -2 \\\\\n3u &= -3 \\\\\nu &= -1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $u=-1, \\,v=1$, which can be expressed as $(-1,1)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509111 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7242848c-3d45-59cd-b531-0ff9de9e07b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509084}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7242848c-3d45-59cd-b531-0ff9de9e07b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509084} :answer-field/id #uuid "580f77f4-bb2d-5fe9-8c7a-de148eb78cf9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509078} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e215f69-7281-5f0a-b1ad-ca14eb46e414" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509070}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e215f69-7281-5f0a-b1ad-ca14eb46e414" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509070} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f423d74-9353-5d5c-8788-04c8f0bcc44d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509095}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cd3b4b3f-b020-5169-9586-17768134232d" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n$\\{-4x + 5y = 10; x + 6y = -17$\n\nFind the solution $(x, y)$ to this system by eliminating the variable $x$.\n\nThe solution is $($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$)$." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $x$ in the first equation is $-4$, while in the second equation it is $1$.\n\nIf we multiply the second equation by $4$, then the $x$-coefficient will become $4$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $-4$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n\\{-4x + 5y = 10; (x + 6y = -17) \\cdot (4)\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $x$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-4x + 5y &= 10 \\\\\n4x + 24y &= -68 \\\\\n(5y + 24y) &= (10 - 68) \\\\\n29y &= -58 \\\\\ny &= -2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $y = -2$. However, we still need to find $x$. To do this, we substitute $y = -2$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx + 6y &= -17 \\\\\nx + 6(-2) &= -17 \\\\\nx - 12 &= -17 \\\\\nx &= -5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=-5, \\,y=-2$, which can be expressed as $(-5,-2)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509114 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12813af6-c484-54ac-9bee-0b9a07a1472c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509055}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "12813af6-c484-54ac-9bee-0b9a07a1472c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509055} :answer-field/id #uuid "23b567cb-7d1b-5181-9ccc-bcb98c7d98fc" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509057} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e284178-f4bc-505f-90f2-2ff6238fd5eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509054}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e284178-f4bc-505f-90f2-2ff6238fd5eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509054} :answer-field/id #uuid "f538230e-e945-5377-a73a-dcace5a3652d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509119}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d400f619-bf7d-5b12-8de8-ccc69c639d78" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n$\\{s + 3t = -14; 3s - t = -2$\n\nFind the solution $(s, t)$ to this system by eliminating the variable $s$.\n\nThe solution is $($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$)$." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $s$ in the first equation is $1$, while in the second equation it is $3$.\n\nIf we multiply the first equation by $-3$, then the $s$-coefficient will become $-3$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $3$ in the second equation.\n\n$$\n\\{(s + 3t = -14) \\cdot (-3); 3s - t = -2\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $s$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-3s - 9t &= 42 \\\\\n3s - t &= -2 \\\\\n(-9t - t) &= (42 - 2) \\\\\n-10t &= 40 \\\\\nt &= -4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $t = -4$. However, we still need to find $s$. To do this, we substitute $t = -4$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ns + 3t &= -14 \\\\\ns + 3(-4) &= -14 \\\\\ns - 12 &= -14 \\\\\ns &= -2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $s=-2, \\,t=-4$, which can be expressed as $(-2,-4)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509115 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2faf14ba-bba7-51c7-9edf-cecfc41c14b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-7, 17)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509060} {:answer/id #uuid "341043a8-156f-5366-9a35-b7d38e44dfa3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{11}{14}, \\frac{10}{7})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509065} {:answer/id #uuid "4aedf174-56a2-5192-a1db-d3ba0e5fc303" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1, 5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509076} {:answer/id #uuid "9632d4fa-7a1a-5278-a13a-d1e219be729e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- \\frac{19}{4}, \\frac{25}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509092} {:answer/id #uuid "d97fab02-f410-5d26-9830-684eabd5761d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4, 5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509116}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4aedf174-56a2-5192-a1db-d3ba0e5fc303" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1, 5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509076} :answer-field/id #uuid "c554ee94-9b1e-56b7-bcce-cdb86ae35436" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509108}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d579d3ab-2a4e-5b62-a685-7b2b44091ebf" :question/problem "Find the solution $(s, t)$ to the following system of equations using the elimination method:\n\n$\\{8s + 6t = 22; 2s + t = 3$\n\n*Hint: Eliminate the variable $s$.*" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $s$ in the first equation is $8$, while in the second equation it is $2$.\n\nIf we multiply the second equation by $-4$, then the $s$-coefficient will become $-8$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $8$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n\\{8s + 6t = 22; (2s + t = 3) \\cdot (-4)\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $s$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n8s + 6t &= 22 \\\\\n-8s - 4t &= -12 \\\\\n(6t - 4t) &= (22 - 12) \\\\\n2t &= 10 \\\\\nt &= 5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $t = 5$. However, we still need to find $s$. To do this, we substitute $t = 5$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2s + t &= 3 \\\\\n2s + (5) &= 3 \\\\\n2s + 5 &= 3 \\\\\n2s &= -2 \\\\\ns &= -1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $s=-1, \\,t=5$, which can be expressed as $(-1,5)$."}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System of Equations by Eliminating the First Variable"}]}
